<!doctype html><html lang="en" class="no-js"><head><meta charset="utf-8"> <!-- begin SEO --><title>About - Jialiang Fan (樊佳亮)</title><meta name="description" content="Jialiang Fan’s academic pages"><link rel="canonical" href="https://jialiangfan.com/"> <script type="application/ld+json"> { "@context" : "http://schema.org", "@type" : "Person", "name" : "Jialiang Fan", "url" : "https://jialiangfan.com", "sameAs" : null } </script> <!-- end SEO --> <!-- Open Graph protocol data (https://ogp.me/), used by social media --><meta property="og:locale" content="en-US"><meta property="og:site_name" content="Jialiang Fan (樊佳亮)"><meta property="og:title" content="About"><meta property="og:url" content="https://jialiangfan.com/"> <!-- end Open Graph protocol --><link href="https://jialiangfan.com/feed.xml" type="application/atom+xml" rel="alternate" title="Jialiang Fan (樊佳亮) Feed"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0"> <script> document.documentElement.className = document.documentElement.className.replace(/\bno-js\b/g, '') + ' js '; </script> <!-- For all browsers --><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://jialiangfan.com/assets/css/main.css"> <!-- start custom head snippets --> <!-- Support for Academicons --><link rel="stylesheet" href="https://jialiangfan.com/assets/css/academicons.css"/> <!-- favicon from https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:OOjs_UI_icon_academic-progressive.svg --><link rel="apple-touch-icon" sizes="180x180" href="https://jialiangfan.com/images/apple-touch-icon-180x180.png"/><link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="https://jialiangfan.com/images/favicon.svg"/><link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="https://jialiangfan.com/images/favicon-32x32.png" sizes="32x32"/><link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="https://jialiangfan.com/images/favicon-192x192.png" sizes="192x192"/><link rel="manifest" href="https://jialiangfan.com/images/manifest.json"/><link rel="icon" href="/images/favicon.ico"/><meta name="theme-color" content="#ffffff"/> <!-- end custom head snippets --></head><body> <!--[if lt IE 9]><div class="notice--danger align-center" style="margin: 0;">You are using an <strong>outdated</strong> browser. Please <a href="http://browsehappy.com/">upgrade your browser</a> to improve your experience.</div><![endif]--><div class="masthead"><div class="masthead__inner-wrap"><div class="masthead__menu"><nav id="site-nav" class="greedy-nav"> <button><span class="navicon"></span></button><ul class="visible-links"><li class="masthead__menu-item masthead__menu-item--lg persist selected"> <a href="https://jialiangfan.com/">Jialiang Fan (樊佳亮)</a></li><li class="masthead__menu-item "> <a href="https://jialiangfan.com/publications/">Projects</a></li><li class="masthead__menu-item "> <a href="https://jialiangfan.com/portfolio/">Code</a></li><li class="masthead__menu-item "> <a href="https://jialiangfan.com/blog/">Blog</a></li><li class="masthead__menu-item "> <a href="https://jialiangfan.com/files/CV_Jialiang_Fan.pdf">CV</a></li><li class="masthead__menu-item "> <a href="https://jialiangfan.com/robots/">Robots</a></li><li class="masthead__menu-item "> <a href="https://jialiangfan.com/life/">Life</a></li><li id="theme-toggle" class="masthead__menu-item persist tail"> <a role="button" aria-labelledby="theme-icon"><i id="theme-icon" class="fa-solid fa-sun" aria-hidden="true" title="toggle theme"></i></a></li></ul><ul class="hidden-links hidden"></ul></nav></div></div></div><div id="main" role="main"><div class="sidebar sticky"><div itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/Person"><div class="author__avatar"> <img src="https://jialiangfan.com/images/profile.jpg" class="author__avatar" alt="Jialiang Fan (樊佳亮)" fetchpriority="high" /></div><div class="author__content"><h3 class="author__name">Jialiang Fan (樊佳亮)</h3><p class="author__bio">PhD student at University of Notre Dame. Research in cyber-physical systems, robotics, reinforcement learning, and safe learning.</p></div><div class="author__urls-wrapper"> <button class="btn btn--inverse">Follow</button><ul class="author__urls social-icons"> <!-- Font Awesome icons / Biographic information --><li class="author__desktop"><i class="fas fa-fw fa-location-dot icon-pad-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>Notre Dame, IN</li><li class="author__desktop"><i class="fas fa-fw fa-building-columns icon-pad-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>University of Notre Dame</li><li><a href="mailto:fjl2401@gmail.com"><i class="fas fa-fw fa-envelope icon-pad-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>Email</a></li><!-- Font Awesome and Academicons icons / Academic websites --><li><a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=6LAGBq8AAAAJ"><i class="ai ai-google-scholar ai-fw icon-pad-right"></i>Google Scholar</a></li><!-- Font Awesome icons / Repositories and software development --><li><a href="https://github.com/JialiangFan"><i class="fab fa-fw fa-github icon-pad-right" aria-hidden="true"></i>GitHub</a></li><!-- Font Awesome icons / Social media --></ul></div></div></div><article class="page" itemscope itemtype="http://schema.org/CreativeWork"><meta itemprop="headline" content="About"><div class="page__inner-wrap"><header><h1 class="page__title" itemprop="headline">About</h1></header><section class="page__content" itemprop="text"><p>I am a PhD student (2024 - present) at <a href="https://www.nd.edu/">University of Notre Dame</a> in the Department of Computer Science and Engineering, supervised by <a href="https://sites.google.com/site/fanxink">Prof. Fanxin Kong</a>. I also work closely with Prof. Insup Lee and Prof. Oleg Sokolsky. I received my B.E. in Software Engineering from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shandong_University">Shandong University</a> in 2019 and my M.S. in Computer Technology from <a href="https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lanzhou_University">Lanzhou University</a> in 2023.</p><p>My research interests include <strong>robot learning</strong>, <strong>cyber-physical systems</strong>, <strong>vision-language-action models</strong>, and <strong>world models</strong>.</p><h2 id="news">News</h2><ul><li><strong>[Sep 2026]</strong> Our paper “Exploiting Fine-Tuning Structures to Improve Adversarial Transferability on Downstream SAM” has been accepted to <strong>NeurIPS 2026</strong>!</li><li><strong>[Aug 2026]</strong> I wrapped up my summer Research Internship at <strong><a href="https://global.abb/">ABB</a></strong> on Aug 14. Huge thanks to my supervisor <strong>Dr. Jianjun Wang</strong> for his full support and recognition throughout!</li><li><strong>[Jun 2026]</strong> I passed my Ph.D. qualifying examination at the University of Notre Dame!</li><li><strong>[May 2026]</strong> Our paper “<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2606.00773">SafeVLA-Bench: A Benchmark for the Success-Safety Gap in Vision-Language-Action Models</a>” is now available on arXiv! (First author)</li><li><strong>[May 2026]</strong> I am honored to be joining <strong><a href="https://global.abb/">ABB</a></strong> as a <strong>Research Intern</strong> this summer — taking my fishing talents to East Beach (Lake Erie awaits)!</li><li><strong>[May 2026]</strong> I received the <strong>Outstanding Teaching Assistant Award</strong> (2025-2026) from the Department of Computer Science and Engineering at the University of Notre Dame!</li><li><strong>[Feb 2026]</strong> Our paper “<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.24235">SafeGen-LLM: Enhancing Safety Generalization in Task Planning for Robotic Systems</a>” is now available on arXiv! (First author)</li><li><strong>[Feb 2026]</strong> Our paper “<a href="https://arxiv.org/abs/2602.16543">Vulnerability Analysis of Safe Reinforcement Learning via Inverse Constrained Reinforcement Learning</a>” is now available on arXiv! (First author)</li><li><strong>[Jan 2026]</strong> Our paper “SafeNet: A Neural-Symbolic Network for Safe Planning in Robotic Systems using Formal Method-Guided LLM Fine-Tuning” has been accepted to <strong>ICRA 2026</strong>! (Second author)</li><li><strong>[Jan 2026]</strong> Our paper “Vulnerability Exploration of Safe Reinforcement Learning in Cyber-Physical Systems via STL Mining” has been accepted to <strong>ICCPS 2026</strong>! (First author)</li><li><strong>[Apr 2025]</strong> I went to Orlando for the SPIE Defense + Commercial Sensing conference.</li><li><strong>[Jun 2024]</strong> I joined the University of Notre Dame as a PhD student supervised by <a href="https://sites.google.com/site/fanxink">Prof. Fanxin Kong</a>.</li></ul><h2 id="project-videos">Project Videos</h2><div class="video-grid-home"><div class="video-card-home"><div class="video-container"> <iframe src="https://www.youtube.com/embed/2XPbGV8ltms" frameborder="0" allowfullscreen="" allow="accelerometer; autoplay; clipboard-write; encrypted-media; gyroscope; picture-in-picture"></iframe></div><h3><a href="/portfolio/project-1/">LLM-based Blocksworld Planning on myCobot 280pi</a></h3><p>Demonstration of LLM-based task planning for block manipulation using the myCobot 280pi robotic arm.</p></div></div><style> .video-grid-home { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fill, minmax(360px, 1fr)); gap: 1.5em; margin-top: 1em; } .video-card-home { border: 1px solid #e0e0e0; border-radius: 8px; overflow: hidden; padding-bottom: 0.5em; } .video-card-home h3 { padding: 0.5em 1em 0; margin: 0; } .video-card-home p { padding: 0 1em; margin: 0.25em 0; font-size: 0.9em; color: #555; } .video-container { position: relative; padding-bottom: 56.25%; height: 0; overflow: hidden; } .video-container iframe { position: absolute; top: 0; left: 0; width: 100%; height: 100%; }</style></section><footer class="page__meta"></footer></div></article></div><div class="page__footer"><footer> <!-- start custom footer snippets --> <a href="/sitemap/">Sitemap</a> <!-- Support for MatJax --> <script defer src="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/polyfill/v3/polyfill.min.js?features=es6"></script> <script defer src="https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mathjax@3/es5/tex-mml-chtml.js" id="MathJax-script"></script> <!-- Support for Mermaid --> <script type="module"> import mermaid from 'https://cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/mermaid@11/dist/mermaid.esm.min.mjs'; mermaid.initialize({startOnLoad:true, theme:'default'}); await mermaid.run({querySelector:'code.language-mermaid'}); </script> <!-- end custom footer snippets --><div class="page__footer-follow"><ul class="social-icons"><li><strong>Follow:</strong></li><li><a href="https://github.com/JialiangFan"><i class="fab fa-github" aria-hidden="true"></i> GitHub</a></li><li><a href="https://jialiangfan.com/feed.xml"><i class="fa fa-fw fa-rss-square" aria-hidden="true"></i> Feed</a></li></ul></div><div class="page__footer-copyright"> &copy; 2026 Jialiang Fan, Powered by <a href="https://jekyllrb.com" rel="nofollow">Jekyll</a> &amp; <a href="https://github.com/academicpages/academicpages.github.io">AcademicPages</a>, a fork of <a href="https://mademistakes.com/work/minimal-mistakes-jekyll-theme/" rel="nofollow">Minimal Mistakes</a>.<br /> Site last updated 2026-09-25<br /> <span id="site-uptime"></span><br /> <span id="busuanzi_container_site_pv" style="display:none;">Total visits: <span id="busuanzi_value_site_pv"></span> &middot; </span> <span id="busuanzi_container_site_uv" style="display:none;">Unique visitors: <span id="busuanzi_value_site_uv"></span></span></div><script async src="//busuanzi.ibruce.info/busuanzi/2.3/busuanzi.pure.mini.js"></script> <script> (function () { var days = Math.floor((Date.now() - new Date('2025-03-17T00:00:00Z')) / 86400000); document.getElementById('site-uptime').textContent = 'This site has been running for ' + days + ' days'; })(); </script></footer></div><script type="module" src="https://jialiangfan.com/assets/js/main.min.js"></script></body></html>
